From: RPi-Mac
Subject: [PATCH] aarch64 jit: make special-mem read/write resolve via the direct
 host mapping instead of the all-NULL UAE bank table

The AArch64 JIT's "special" memory path (used for I/O / distrust / the
B2_JIT_ALL_SPECIAL_MEM override) dispatches through regs.mem_banks[adr>>16],
calling a per-bank read/write callback. In BasiliskII's flat direct-addressing
build there is no UAE addrbank table: compiler_init() fills the JIT's mem_banks
array entirely with NULL and nothing ever populates it. The bank dispatch
therefore loads a NULL bank pointer and dereferences it (LDR [NULL+offset]),
which segfaults on the first L2-native special access. Concretely, with
B2_JIT_ALL_SPECIAL_MEM=1 the JIT cleared CLKNOMEM and then died deterministically
in the Slot Manager at guest 0x0404b0c0 (`addal (52,a3),a3`, A3 -> NuBus
0xf0000000): host=(nil), and the compiled-code SEGV recovery missed and crashed.
Earlier special accesses only survived because they happened to run as
interpreter fallbacks.

Since the bank table is vestigial here, route the special path through the same
safe direct host mapping the "real" path uses (LDR [R_MEMSTART + adr] with the
lazy-0xFF I/O/NuBus mappings). Reads then see the same bus values the
interpreter does and the NuBus null-deref is gone; the JIT now advances past the
crash into video-driver init. This only affects the special path (default JIT
and the pure interpreter are unchanged).

--- a/BasiliskII/src/uae_cpu_2026/compiler/compemu_support_arm.cpp
+++ b/BasiliskII/src/uae_cpu_2026/compiler/compemu_support_arm.cpp
@@ -4707,7 +4707,14 @@
 
 static inline void writemem_special(int address, int source, int offset)
 {
-    jnf_MEM_WRITEMEMBANK(address, source, offset);
+    // See readmem_special: the all-NULL regs.mem_banks dispatch would deref
+    // NULL, so write straight to the mapped host memory instead.
+    if (offset == SIZEOF_VOID_P * 4)             // word
+        writemem_real(address, source, 2);
+    else if (offset == SIZEOF_VOID_P * 5)        // byte
+        writemem_real(address, source, 1);
+    else                                         // longword (offset 3*P)
+        writemem_real(address, source, 4);
 }
 
 void writebyte(int address, int source)
@@ -4777,7 +4784,24 @@
 
 static inline void readmem_special(int address, int dest, int offset)
 {
-    jnf_MEM_READMEMBANK(dest, address, offset);
+    // BasiliskII uses flat direct addressing; regs.mem_banks is an all-NULL
+    // table (see compiler_init), so the UAE-style bank dispatch in
+    // jnf_MEM_READMEMBANK dereferences NULL and crashes on the first L2-native
+    // special access (e.g. the NuBus slot probe at guest 0x0404b0c0). Route the
+    // access through the safe direct host mapping instead; lazy-fill backs the
+    // IO/NuBus ranges, so reads see the same bus values the interpreter does.
+    if (offset == SIZEOF_VOID_P * 6) {           // xlateaddr (get_n_addr)
+        if (currprefs.address_space_24)
+            jnf_MEM_GETADR24_OFF(dest, address);
+        else
+            jnf_MEM_GETADR_OFF(dest, address);
+    } else if (offset == SIZEOF_VOID_P * 1) {    // word
+        readmem_real(address, dest, 2);
+    } else if (offset == SIZEOF_VOID_P * 2) {    // byte
+        readmem_real(address, dest, 1);
+    } else {                                     // longword (offset 0)
+        readmem_real(address, dest, 4);
+    }
 }
 
 void readbyte(int address, int dest)
